{"nodes": [{"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_recovery_error_recovery", "label": "Error recovery and change handling supplement", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol-recovery.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loaded only on session resume or when a change event is detected mid-stage, as a supplement rather than a replacement, so the main protocol stays the common path and recovery prose does not weigh on every stage."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_recovery_recovery_read_order", "label": "Recovery source read order (artefacts, diary, audit, state, runtime graph)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol-recovery.md", "source_location": "### Recovery sources and read order", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Outputs first, notes second, timeline third, cursor fourth, summary last \u2014 the same way a human picks up someone else's half-finished work. The append-only audit trail is canonical and the other four are reconciled against it on disagreement; the previous session's conversation buffer is unrecoverable by design, so re-orientation comes from these five sources instead of an attempted chat reconstruction."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_recovery_error_severity_levels", "label": "Error severity levels and escalation guidelines", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol-recovery.md", "source_location": "### Error Severity Levels", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Critical and High stop and ask immediately with no guessing; Medium attempts resolution then asks; Low is handled silently and logged \u2014 so human interruption is rationed to cases where a wrong guess would corrupt the output."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_recovery_contradiction_recovery", "label": "Contradictory-inputs recovery (never self-resolve)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol-recovery.md", "source_location": "### Contradictory inputs recovery", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When inputs from different stages contradict, the contradiction is quoted from both sources and the user decides which takes priority; the agent explicitly must not resolve it by choosing an interpretation, because a silent choice hides a decision the human owns."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_recovery_new_material_mid_stage", "label": "New reference material mid-stage is evidence, not a routing instruction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol-recovery.md", "source_location": "### New reference material supplied mid-stage", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supplying material is not a request to advance: new material sharpens the current design rather than signalling the design is done, so the workflow stays on the current stage and unit instead of skipping remaining design stages or jumping to code generation."}], "edges": [{"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_recovery_error_recovery", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_stage_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol-recovery.md", "source_location": "# Stage Protocol: Error Recovery & Change Handling", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_recovery_error_recovery", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_recovery_recovery_read_order", "relation":